WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.483
Idea. Think of a busy office. Someone buys stamps, pays a taxi fare, or buys cleaning materials. These are tiny cash payments, and there are lots of them. Writing every one in the main cash book would fill it with clutter.

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:25.278
So businesses keep a petty cash book. Petty means small. It records small cash payments made from a float kept in the office, separate from the main cash book.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:39.363
Why keep one? It keeps the main cash book free of small entries. It saves the chief cashier's time and trains a junior. It controls small spending, and its analysis columns group the spending by type.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:48.946
Method. First, choose a purpose from the list. Each mark needs a different idea, so never say the same thing twice in other words.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:01:00.143
If the question says explain, add the effect on the business. For example: a junior handles small payments, so the chief cashier has more time for larger items.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:13.478
If the question says discuss, give a drawback too, such as extra work or the risk of cash being lost or stolen. Then make a judgement for that business. A very small business may not need one.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:26.469
Worked example. Here is a real question from November 2024. State two purposes of maintaining a petty cash book. Two marks, so we need two different ideas.

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:33.074
Purpose one: to keep many small payments out of the main cash book, so that book has fewer entries.

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:41.254
Purpose two: to keep a check on small office expenses, so spending on things like postage and cleaning is controlled.

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:53.071
Check that the two points are different. One is about the main cash book, the other is about control. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:02:04.930
Common mistake. A common mistake is giving the same purpose twice in different words. Saving the cashier's time and making the cashier less busy are one idea.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.850
Another is describing what the book looks like, instead of why it is kept.

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:20.785
Your turn. Now you try. Omar runs a busy dental clinic. Explain one reason why he should keep a petty cash book. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:37.200
Answer. One answer: the receptionist can make the small payments from petty cash, so Omar's chief cashier has more time for the larger payments. Another good answer is fewer entries in the main cash book, so it is easier to check.

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:46.879
Remember: choose different purposes, develop each with so, and for discuss give a drawback and a judgement. Now try the practice questions.
